        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b20d8c39a0f0467787157f1961d0fafd",
      "statement": "In the default MeshTopology, the peer with the higher numeric peer ID creates the WebRTC offer to the lower ID to avoid offer collisions.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://client/src/topology/meshTopology.ts#L32-L33",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e72de8cd7442894af8f52f1bca121810d1b57da2295dae016e4107332e792576:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_ad2d5b16d6b245e3a8a62a28587ca8d6",
      "statement": "SDP offers and answers are exchanged as protobuf ClientMessage/ServerMessage frames over the signaling WebSocket, and ICE candidates are flushed to the wire after a waitIceCandidatesTimeout (default 2000 ms) instead of being held indefinitely.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://client/src/const.ts#L39-L51",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e72614d259fb4a38815534354c42033508ac162405fc723b4353d5ac23054b4f:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://client/src/zeroHub.ts#L1656-L1765",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f0e2f9da3f452348f0b44f25a6dba76ad9e5efb29a3d039212ca0ac76bb3ebd8:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_4bc725d0e12f4379ac5b0f092ffd5b66",
      "statement": "When a peer joins a hub, the hub assigns it a monotonically increasing numeric ID via an atomic counter, broadcasts a PeerJoinedMessage to existing peers, and sends the new peer a HubInfoMessage containing its own peer ID, hub metadata, and the existing peer roster; the join signal is marshaled before the peer is registered in storage, so a marshal failure is a no-op and never leaves a half-registered peer.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/pkg/hub/hub.go#L99-L171",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f26e757f59106578f4cd70f5aeeae01afefe70d76a9a54f34fe534f63b7b274c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f7fafa749519416eb6ce4c151c5edb57",
      "statement": "Both hubs and the peers within them are stored behind a generic storage.Storage[T] interface (Add, GetAll, Get, Delete, IsEmpty) with in-memory and Gache backends, selected by the APP_HUB_STORAGE and APP_PEER_STORAGE config values.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/pkg/storage/storage.go",
          "version": "repo-file-v1:sha256:8bd2f4d11c2d75084369a8b79d9fcbcf518f903238adf1af50d98fe33166ecf4"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_81cb264281c3495a995af79297c2c7d4",
      "statement": "The client exposes a pluggable Topology interface (init + onPeerStatusChange) that decides per-peer how to set up data channels, media tracks, and who sends the offer; MeshTopology and SFUTopology are the two built-in implementations.",
      "evidence": [
        {
